<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Deep Learning for Early Identification of Neurodegenerative Diseases)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Abstract)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Degenerative neurological conditions including Alzheimer's, Parkinson's, and Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis are diseases characterized by the progressive degeneration of neurons several years before any clinical appearance. One of the biggest challenges in modern medicine is the early identification of these diseases. Deep learning is one field of artificial intelligence that has been able to demonstrate remarkable results in identifying patterns in biomedical sciences, thus facilitating early diagnosis [1], [5]. This article presents an overview of how deep learning techniques have been utilized in diagnosing neurodegenerative diseases at their early stages.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Introduction)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
