<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (2. Deep Learning in Neurodegenerative Disease Detection)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (The deep learning \(DL\) models utilize artificial neural networks that use multiple layers to represent the hierarchical nature of data [6]. DL is more advanced than conventional machine learning because the former does not need any feature extraction process to enhance accuracy of predictions [5], [6].Examples of areas in which DL-based techniques have demonstrated effectiveness include the following:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Identification and prediction of diseases [6])
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
