253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 131 0 R
/T (CASC-M | VOL.7, ISSUE 2 |MAR-APR, 2026)
/E (CASC-M | VOL.7, ISSUE 2 |MAR-APR, 2026)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Deep learning algorithms are essential for analysis of various kinds of medical datasets for early diagnosis of neurodegenerative diseases. Among the most popular models, one can mention Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\). This algorithm is very commonly used for image datasets such as MRI scans or PET. CNN uses numerous filters in order to extract crucial spatial features such as edges, texture, and other structural changes in a brain. Thanks to this, early diagnosis of brain atrophy can be made [5], [7].The next set of models worth considering includes recurrent neural networks \(RNN\), as well as advanced versions of the latter such as LSTM networks. This model is able to preserve the information about the previous state and is therefore able to analyze temporal data including patient history, cognition scores, and repeat measures in order to evaluate the disease progression [3], [6]. More advanced and complex models to be mentioned in this context are transformer models. Thanks to the use of attention mechanisms, this algorithm is able to focus on the most relevant information and, consequently, to enhance predictions for larger and multimodal datasets including imaging, clinical, and genomics data [3],[6].Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\) are widely used for analyzing medical images such as MRI and PET scans. They extract important spatial features like edges and textures to detect brain abnormalities. Deep learning models such as CNN, RNN, and transformers are widely used in medical applications. Their functions are summarized in Table 1. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (4. Models Used)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (the initial development of brain changes, including amyloid plaque buildup and hippocampal atrophy [2], [7]. The occurrence of these physiological changes usually takes place years ahead of the memory impairments, making it possible to diagnose and intervene in the disease. For Parkinson's disease, deep learning algorithms are utilized to evaluate motion-related characteristics like tremors, voice variations, gait disturbances, and penmanship [4], [6]. Patients can thus be evaluated through non-invasive means such as wearables and voice records.Moreover, deep learning can be employed in identifying early signs and tracking the development of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis \(ALS\). Using clinical records and neurological markers, these deep learning models can determine motor neuron degeneration and ALS progression rate [3], [6].)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (5. Applications)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Deep learning approaches have been successfully employed in disease identification across several types of medical and behavioral datasets. For instance, during the early diagnosis of Alzheimer's disease, CNNs can be used to assess MRI and PET scans to detect )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
