341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1205 0 R
/E (Traditional interconnect technologies are increasingly unable to meet these bandwidth demands efficiently, creating a strong incentive for the adoption of photonic solutions.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1206 0 R
/E (Hyperscale data centers, operated by major technology companies, are at the forefront of this transition. These facilities prioritize performance-per-watt and scalability, both of which align closely with the strengths of photonic interconnects.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1207 0 R
/T (Emergence of Co-Packaged Optics \(CPO\))
/E (Emergence of Co-Packaged Optics \(CPO\))
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1208 0 R
/E (One of the most significant technological developments in this domain is Co-Packaged Optics \(CPO\). In this approach, photonic components are integrated directly alongside electronic processors within the same package, rather than being connected via external optical modules.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1209 0 R
/E (This integration reduces the distance that electrical signals must travel before being converted into optical signals, thereby minimizing energy loss and latency. As a result, CPO offers substantial improvements in both performance and power efficiency compared to traditional pluggable optical transceivers [5][8].)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1210 0 R
/E (CPO is increasingly being viewed as a key enabler for next-generation data center architectures, particularly as bandwidth requirements continue to scale exponentially.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1211 0 R
/T (Role of AI in Accelerating Photonics Adoption)
/E (Role of AI in Accelerating Photonics Adoption)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1212 0 R
/E (Artificial intelligence is not only a driver of demand but also a contributor to innovation in photonics. Research into photonic neural networks suggests that optical systems could be used to accelerate certain types of computations, particularly those involving matrix operations and parallel data processing [6].)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1213 0 R
/E (While still in early stages, such approaches indicate the potential for photonics to move beyond interconnects and play a direct role in computation itself. Efficient handling of parallel workloads and reduction of speculative execution overheads are critical in such environments, further motivating the adoption of high-bandwidth, low-latency photonic interconnects [4][6][9][10].)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (Looking ahead, several trends are expected to shape the evolution of photonic integrated circuits:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
