367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1223 0 R
/E (With advantages such as high bandwidth density, superior energy efficiency, and immunity to electromagnetic interference, PICs are particularly well-suited for the demands of AI-driven workloads and large-scale data center operations [1][2]. At the same time, challenges related to manufacturing complexity and lack of standardization continue to hinder widespread adoption.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1224 0 R
/E (The progress of silicon photonics over the next decade will depend on overcoming these barriers through innovation in materials, fabrication techniques, and ecosystem development. If successful, photonic technologies have the potential to extend beyond data centers and become integral to edge computing, communication systems, and even computational architectures themselves.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
