404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (In contrast, semiconductor quantum dot platforms are more sensitive to the overall system scale and node count. These topological features act as identifiable scaffolds that determine how environmental noise propagates through the system, either accelerating or slowing the rate at which the circuit loses its coherence and historical data. \(Fu et al., 2026\)                         )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E ( an exponential number of measurement shots is required to resolve a training direction, effectively destroying any potential for quantum speedup. This barrier is independent of the parameter initialization strategy, meaning that once a circuit reaches a certain depth-to-qubit ratio, the hardware noise universally erases the functional history of the parameters. \(Wang et al., 2021\))
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (The Taxonomy of Scalability Barriers)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
